.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-context-current 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-context\-current \- Prints the current context\*(Aqs name and nothing else, for a shell prompt
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring context current\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the current context\*(Aqs name and nothing else, for a shell prompt
.PP
Prints nothing and exits 1 if no context is current.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
When to colour log lines and the picker: auto, always, or never

`auto`, the default, colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
